# Local dev API base (docs/development/local-dev.md). The Vite dev server proxies
# /api -> this origin, so app code keeps using relative /api/v1 URLs and the
# browser only ever talks to http://localhost:5173.
#
# Deliberately NOT set: `apiBase()` (src/api/client.ts) would then return this
# absolute origin and the app would call http://localhost:5080 CROSS-ORIGIN.
# The API configures no CORS policy at all (it never needs one — every
# deployment is same-origin behind the single Caddy), so the browser blocks
# every read with "Failed to fetch" and the dev loop looks like a dead API.
# Unset, the client sends relative URLs, Vite proxies them, and dev matches the
# deployed same-origin shape. Set it only to point at a REMOTE API that does
# serve CORS headers.
#VITE_API_BASE=http://localhost:5080
